1
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,120
Just step back and try it.

2
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:12,720
Me.

3
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:45,980
You understand, right?

4
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,940
I know, I know.

5
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,940
Got it? Then shut up and follow me!

6
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,540
I'm an actress, you know.

7
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,280
Reiko of Kameari.

8
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:14,680
Senpai, what are we gonna do now?

9
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:20,580
In the end, it was the final race,
and we're completely broke.

10
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,820
I'm hungry.

11
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,640
Horse racing is a man's dream.

12
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:28,320
Doesn't the saying go,
"A samurai may go hungry, but he keeps his head high"?

13
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:31,860
What's that? I'm not a samurai, though!

14
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,800
Men are such idiots, aren't they?

15
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:37,280
Seriously, idiots.

16
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,490
Even without any talent for horse racing,

17
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:44,120
you never learn, do you?
What a hopeless fool.

18
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,960
Fool.

19
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:52,180
Shut up! Be quiet! Don't write on the ground!
What would you women know?

20
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,680
Then what's this?

21
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,840
A Pain Race trifecta ticket?!

22
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:00,140
W-what?! Hey! How did you get that?!

23
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,480
I only bought one hundred yen's worth yesterday,
when I went along with the traffic division, and it hit.

24
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,520
Call it a woman's intuition?

25
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,540
Hold on a second!

26
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:15,580
I'm sick of it.
Being a man, everything about it.

27
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:20,540
A buffet? All you can eat,
500 yen per person including tax?

28
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,000
But that was money out of my reach.

29
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,000
That's right.

30
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,570
She told me to use it when I was in trouble,

31
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:37,100
and Grandma slipped a thousand-yen
bill into my charm for me.

32
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:37,940
Really?!

33
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,120
Yes, so with this buffet...

34
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,260
This one's women-only!

35
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,120
What?!

36
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,460
So only women can eat for 500 yen

37
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,600
Why?! Why can't men go?!

38
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:56,600
Well, men wouldn't make back their money,
would they?

39
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,140
That's not true!

40
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:01,500
There are men with small appetites,
and there are women who eat a lot too!

41
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,220
I suppose that's logical, but...

42
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:09,600
Down with women-only!
I'll fight for true gender equality!

43
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:27,200
Looks delicious!
Well, let's dig in, Sako-san.

44
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:30,040
So this is how you fight, senpai?

45
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,600
That's right. This is true gender equality.

46
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,220
Itadakimasu!

47
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:40,780
Hey, senpai, could you eat a
little more ladylike, please?

48
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:44,400
Relax, everyone's too busy
stuffing their faces to notice.

49
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,580
Ladylike? Yeah right, nom nom nom.

50
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:52,020
Really? Then I'll join in too.

51
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:58,260
Our battle has only just begun.

52
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,540
That's right, isn't it?

53
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:10,960
Chomp!

54
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,560
Chomp!

55
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,120
Chomp!

56
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:12,260
Chomp!

57
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:12,780
Chomp!

58
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:12,840
Chomp!

59
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,040
Chomp!

60
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,360
Chomp!

61
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:13,460
Chomp!

62
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:13,800
Chomp!

63
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:13,900
*Chomp*

64
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,040
*Chomp*

65
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:16,680
*Chomp*

66
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:16,880
*Chomp*

67
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,320
*Chomp*

68
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:17,780
*Chomp*

69
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:17,820
*Chomp*

70
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:19,460
*Chomp*

71
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,900
*Chomp*

72
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,580
*Chomp*

73
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,740
*Chomp*

74
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:26,500
*Chomp*

75
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:30,360
*Chomp*

76
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:34,680
*Chomp*

77
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:39,780
*Chomp*

78
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:44,060
Aaaaah! Sorry, sorry!

79
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:48,180
Here's my card.

80
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:57,060
I'm a producer at a TV station. We'd
really love for you to appear in our drama.

81
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,760
There, you're all done.

82
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,340
Senpai, you look beautiful.

83
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:09,160
R-really?

84
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,920
W-wh-wh-wh, same as the TV show Hanayama...

85
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:18,320
Who's the lead in the TV drama I'm in?

86
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,800
The lead is Shiori Momoyama.

87
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:24,260
The actress who's number one on the
list of women everyone wants to marry...

88
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:27,140
Alright, we're going for the real take now.

89
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,440
Wow, it's the real Shiori Momoyama!

90
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,420
I can't eat all this.

91
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:39,180
Takako, you're such a light eater!

92
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:41,280
Okay, good.

93
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,100
So what's my role?

94
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:47,680
You'll play Takako,
the lead, just like Shiori.

95
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,000
Please, I'm counting on you.

96
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,480
Well then, good luck.

97
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:58,240
I'm Momoyama. Nice to meet you.

98
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,600
I'm Reiko Kameari. Nice to meet you.

99
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:06,005
As expected of the most popular actress.

100
00:06:06,055 --> 00:06:08,520
She's so beautiful, she hardly seems real.

101
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,020
Do I just eat this?

102
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,042
Just go all out and say it. Then -

103
00:06:15,092 --> 00:06:17,340
We're going straight to the take,
no rehearsal.

104
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:19,480
Ready, action!

105
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:37,940
Sorry. Yeah, uh-huh.

106
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:43,320
Oh, yes, OK!

107
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,520
What a weird driver.

108
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:54,880
Sorry. I can't drink alcohol.

109
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:58,787
In other words, Reiko-kun,
in the protagonist's imagination,

110
00:06:58,837 --> 00:07:01,960
I want you to play another Takako.

111
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:06,660
That's 235 yen per one.

112
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,080
Mm-hmm.

113
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,660
Mm.

114
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:14,780
Hehe.

115
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,620
Yeah, let's go for one more!

116
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,200
Mm, mm, mm.

117
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:25,080
After eating all that,
how do you still have room for a bento?

118
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:27,500
If you're not going to eat it, I'll take it.

119
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:30,180
I'm having this for tonight's dinner.

120
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:31,900
That's right.

121
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,280
The producer entrusted me with this.

122
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:37,180
I asked him to pay my
fee in cash right away.

123
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:38,540
Let's see, let's see.

124
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:46,680
Eating for free, getting a bento, and even being paid?
It's like a dream, Hayako-chan.

125
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:49,800
Right, and the moment we did that,
our luck turned around, didn't it?

126
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,000
Reiko-senpai.

127
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,980
Here you go.

128
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:59,380
My screen time has increased,
so please don't leave yet.

129
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:03,800
Also, I have lines next,
so please read through the script.

130
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:07,580
The jelly-style one is amazing,
isn't it, Center?

131
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:17,280
It's already started! What, what? Shiori Momoyama's drama starts today.
They say it'll break every convention we've known so far.

132
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:23,980
The buzz beforehand is incredible!
Hey, Takako-san, today's on me, so eat lots.

133
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,220
Please, eat up. Aaaah.

134
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:33,160
But I can't possibly eat this much.
Takako-san is such a small eater

135
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,100
Not enough to fill us up

136
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:56,760
This, this is the good part, this drama.

137
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,500
"Not enough to fill us up."

138
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,240
My wife watches it too.

139
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:03,080
That's the one where she says
"not enough to fill me up," right?

140
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:03,600
Yeah, yeah.

141
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:08,360
The actress in Shiori Momoyama's
fantasy scenes is a masterpiece.

142
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,820
You know, she looks exactly like Ryo-chan.

143
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:14,580
The actress who looks like a senior officer?

144
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:18,040
Right, they said she's a face you've seen somewhere before,
didn't they?

145
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:23,520
It was being talked about around
the station this morning, too.

146
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,640
Is that drama really that interesting?

147
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:29,220
It's a drama about a
woman who's a big eater.

148
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:31,720
It's a drama where she
just wolfs it all down.

149
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,440
That's a weird drama, isn't it, senior?

150
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,140
It's not a weird drama.

151
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:42,260
It's not about Ms. Momoyama.
It's about Takako's suppressed emotions

152
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:47,380
being unraveled,
depicted in a humorous and fantastical way.

153
00:09:47,380 --> 00:09:50,740
It is absolutely not a
weird drama like you two say.

154
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,420
I see.

155
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Hey, senior, did you shave your beard?

156
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,300
Now that you mention it,
there's no hair on your arms either.

157
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:02,760
Well, men these days have to
take care of unwanted hair too.

158
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,340
You haven't done that yet,
have you, Ryotsu-san?

159
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:08,500
You're late, Honda!
I'll be out for about four hours.

160
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:12,280
I have my reasons, so my schedule will be irregular for a while.
Bear with me.

161
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,600
Senior, you're acting strange, aren't you?

162
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:20,560
You're acting pretty strange.

163
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:34,640
This is the first time in my life
I've been this popular with girls.

164
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:37,700
Don't just suddenly stop talking to me like that,
Reiko-senpai!

165
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:39,980
Good morning.

166
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,380
Shiori-chan,
open this up and hurry it along.

167
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:47,840
At this rate,
we won't finish filming today, Producer.

168
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:49,580
That's bad.

169
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,120
What happened?

170
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:55,580
Reiko-chan! The princess is apparently in a foul mood,
and I'm at my wit's end.

171
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,240
Senpai,
you're on the night shift today, right?

172
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:01,500
If I can't get back to the set,
that's going to be a problem.

173
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:04,200
My turn finally came around, and now this.

174
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:07,120
I won't let some popular
actress's whims push me around.

175
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:08,560
Wait, why?

176
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,300
Hey, you! Open this door!

177
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:13,720
Please stop.

178
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:16,540
Is Shiori really so delicate, unlike you?

179
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:20,140
If you're not going to open up,
then I have my own plans.

180
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,780
Gyaaaah!

181
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:24,820
Aaah...

182
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:28,580
Reiko, are you okay?

183
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,580
I'm fine.

184
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:32,460
I'm fine.

185
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:44,300
So, in short,
what's the reason you're sulking?

186
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,100
Me, a supporting player,
ended up in the spotlight.

187
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:51,200
If it's just something silly like being annoyed,
don't worry about it.

188
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:54,340
Since you and I don't have
overlapping characters either,

189
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:57,620
I think we can coexist
just fine in show business.

190
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:01,240
Well, I can't promise you the
queen's throne in Rendra, though.

191
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,020
I'm not worried about that.

192
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:05,600
I see.

193
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:08,160
I got dumped.

194
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,880
I got dumped, me.

195
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:14,400
I can hardly believe that.

196
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,120
Well, that's a shocking phenomenon.

197
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,080
So, who's the guy?

198
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:23,300
Wait, isn't it Perry, the vocalist of that popular
rock band you were rumored to be linked with?

199
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:28,620
Yeah, we were both so busy we
could hardly find time to meet.

200
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:32,000
Then he told me he'd
fallen for someone else.

201
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,840
Win him back.
You'd have no trouble with that, right?

202
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:38,140
She's someone I've even co-starred
with in a commercial before.

203
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:40,560
She's a talent six years younger than me.

204
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,660
Wait, is it Monaco, the gravure queen?

205
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,440
That was the turning point, then.

206
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,480
You know a lot about it, Reiko.

207
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:52,000
Women's intuition.

208
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:56,480
I read every entertainment column in the sports papers,
after all.

209
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,620
Right from when he started dating me,

210
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:02,680
he was apparently seeing her too,
at the same time.

211
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:06,060
What are you saying?
You mean he was two-timing you?

212
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:10,000
So it wasn't "how enviable"?

213
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,460
What a terrible guy.

214
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:13,400
What do you want to do?

215
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,260
Do you want to get back together with Perry?

216
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,800
But still,
it's infuriating to let it go like this.

217
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,380
Of course.

218
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:25,760
Alright, leave this to me.

219
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:27,540
What are you going to do?

220
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,460
I'll make a fool of him.

221
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,980
Reiko, you're quite the interesting one,
aren't you?

222
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:38,260
In return,
just focus on getting through this drama.

223
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:41,840
Thirty million viewers across
the country are waiting for you.

224
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,560
Got it?

225
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:46,900
Got it.

226
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:48,680
Thanks.

227
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:56,960
Hey, you!

228
00:13:56,960 --> 00:14:02,320
These two are getting
along better and better.

229
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:09,980
That's a wrap, thank you for your hard work.

230
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:12,060
I can't take it anymore.

231
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,580
Let's hurry, Reiko-senpai.

232
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,920
Excuse me for leaving first.

233
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:21,020
Before we head back to the police box,
there's just one place I want to stop by.

234
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:24,600
I feel like the wanko soba
is going to come back up.

235
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:27,820
By the way, Perry-san.

236
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,240
There are rumors going around that
you and Shiori Momoyama broke up.

237
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,720
What's the truth of the matter?

238
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:37,000
Love is a fleeting mirage, isn't it?

239
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,460
I'm totally dizzy over her for my new song.

240
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,880
Isn't there some real person
who inspired the woman in here?

241
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,600
The answer is yes.

242
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,165
And then...

243
00:14:47,215 --> 00:14:50,380
Because I'm an artist.

244
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:54,540
Some are already spreading rumors
about a new romance, though.

245
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,200
Right now, I'm waiting for
Translation>
a goddess to appear and heal my wounded heart.

246
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,820
a goddess to appear and
heal my wounded heart.

247
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:03,540
Is that so?

248
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:07,080
Then how about me?

249
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,400
Y-you're Shiori's...

250
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:13,320
Don't you dare two-time Shiori,
you son of a bitch!

251
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:17,660
That hurts!

252
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,460
Hey, you there!

253
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,540
What do you think you're doing to our Perry?

254
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,260
You're the manager?

255
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,040
Yes.

256
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,800
I don't know if he's a rocker
or a shocker or whatever,

257
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:29,080
but if you're his manager,
teach this young punk

258
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:31,000
some proper manners, won't you?

259
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,540
Yes.

260
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,600
If he tries to pick up girls again,

261
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,280
I'll be back, you hear me?

262
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,460
Sorry for the trouble.

263
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:50,960
This will surely make
Reiko even more popular.

264
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,080
Killing two birds with one stone,
that's what this is.

265
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,800
It's a message from Shiori-chan!

266
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:06,580
Reiko-san, could you spare a little
time after tomorrow's location shoot?

267
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:12,560
Of course, OK! Not just a little, I'll keep you
company all night long, Reiko, you know I will!

268
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:26,140
Top celebrities really are different,
aren't they?

269
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,060
The night view is gorgeous.

270
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:29,920
And I don't have any shoots tomorrow,

271
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:31,820
so why don't you stay
over tonight if you like?

272
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:32,940
Really?

273
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,100
Of course.

274
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:37,100
Since I caused you so much
trouble this time because of me,

275
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,180
I wanted to apologize and thank you.

276
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:41,280
Thank you, Reiko.

277
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:43,120
It's fine, really.

278
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,140
Don't worry about it.

279
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:46,380
I've had my fill of that
type of cheap guy too...

280
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:50,380
Forget about that grudge uh...
that's not what matters.

281
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:53,280
This is the latest model, right?

282
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,260
Why won't it turn on?

283
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,873
It's been acting up for a few days now,

284
00:16:58,923 --> 00:17:00,760
I wonder if it broke.

285
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,400
Could you lend me a
screwdriver if you have one?

286
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,260
Can you fix it?

287
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:14,200
Wow, Reiko, you can do anything, can't you?

288
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,180
Well, yeah.

289
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:18,940
It smells great.

290
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:23,340
Shiori, your food is delicious.
You're such a good cook.

291
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,560
Would you like a little more wine?

292
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,080
Not just a little, a lot.

293
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:33,560
Reiko, there's a jacuzzi bath here.

294
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,240
Let's take a bath together later.

295
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:49,280
It feels better without the towel, you know.

296
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:54,120
Are you sure?
I'm hairy and muscular, so I'm embarrassed.

297
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:57,280
I have plenty of complexes too.

298
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:00,440
That's a really nasty dig, you know.

299
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,200
I'm glad I got to meet you, Reiko.

300
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:10,440
It's hard to make friends you can
trust in the entertainment world.

301
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:16,020
You're my friend, aren't you, Reiko?

302
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:18,920
Let's stay friends forever.

303
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:21,000
Of course.

304
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,340
Reiko, you're bleeding from your nose.

305
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,160
Oh no, I think I'm overheated.

306
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:28,220
I'll go get some ice.

307
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,980
Are you okay, Reiko?

308
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:34,080
I'll get out first.

309
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:37,220
Reiko.

310
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:39,020
I'm fine.

311
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,580
Excuse me for going first.

312
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:52,800
I drank so much, yet I'm not sleepy at all.

313
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,840
If we keep this up,
I won't be able to keep up.

314
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:05,280
Reiko, apparently Ryotsu Kankichi from Kameari is coming
today to be the one-day chief at Katsushika station.

315
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:05,740
What?

316
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:08,500
Really, maybe I should go get his autograph.

317
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:10,840
It's fine, Mister Ryotsu.

318
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:13,880
Hey, what's this about
being a one-day chief?

319
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:17,400
I'm sure I turned that
offer down before, though.

320
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:20,700
The drama's producer said
it would be good publicity.

321
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:22,860
Apparently he went ahead and
arranged it without asking.

322
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:24,100
What are we supposed to do!

323
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:27,560
Isn't this risky? We have to do it, though.

324
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:29,620
Of course it'll get found out, you know.

325
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:32,920
Well, there's a saying
about living the good life.

326
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,220
There's a chance we'll be fine,
you never know.

327
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:36,760
Look, this one's good, right?

328
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,340
Ryotsu, perfect timing.

329
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,260
Chief, what is it?

330
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:45,880
Would you come with me
to Katsushika Station now?

331
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:48,920
Co-starring with Kameari Ryo-san.

332
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:51,540
Right, have you seen it?

333
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,400
It really does look just like him.

334
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,760
The station chief especially
wants you and Ryo-san

335
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,980
to take a PR photo together,
all three of you.

336
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:05,580
Excuse me.

337
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:10,060
So that's how it is. Reiko Akimoto is
apparently going to be a little late.

338
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,360
I'm just going to the restroom for a moment.

339
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:13,920
Hurry up.

340
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:22,460
I'm not letting all our hard work go down
the drain over something this trivial.

341
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:29,580
The women's restroom is out of order, you see.
Sorry, Sauce.

342
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:31,650
Reiko Akimoto.

343
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:35,780
I hereby appoint you one-day
police chief of Katsushika Station.

344
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,120
We're counting on you.

345
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,400
Yes, I'll do my best.

346
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:49,100
Where on earth did Ryotsu go?

347
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,580
Excuse me for a moment.

348
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,580
If we can just get through this part.

349
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:00,740
It's not like that.

350
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:02,020
Don't pass it on to me.

351
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:06,820
Well, the moment I became a man again,
this is what happens.

352
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:08,920
What's wrong, Komachin?

353
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:14,400
Senpai, I mean, Reiko-san,

354
00:21:14,450 --> 00:21:16,180
the chief and the others
are looking for you.

355
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:18,540
What on earth do you want me to do?

356
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:19,420
Reiko-san?

357
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:24,540
Uh, Shiori-chan, what's wrong?

358
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:29,205
I was called in as a special
guest to surprise Reiko-san,

359
00:21:29,255 --> 00:21:30,680
but I got found out first.

360
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,200
I'm so shocked I think I'm going to die.

361
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,780
Once I find that savage,
I'm not going to let him off easy.

362
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:41,400
Look! It's Shiori Momoyama and Reiko!

363
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:46,020
Eek, I'm a huge fan! Please shake my hand!

364
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:51,320
You beat us to a pulp
just a minute ago, though.

365
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,300
Okay, that's a wrap!

366
00:21:55,180 --> 00:21:58,440
Ohara, still no sign of that Ryotsu?

367
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,160
I'm terribly sorry.

368
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:01,900
Please wait just a little longer.

369
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:05,700
Ignoring the Chief's orders?
Ryotsu, you've got some nerve.

370
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:07,840
I'm just going to freshen up my makeup.

371
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:15,300
Oi, Ryotsu! Where have you been?

372
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:18,060
I think I got food poisoning.

373
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:19,500
Ow ow

374
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:21,620
You're pale. Are you all right?

375
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:23,780
You should probably see a doctor.

376
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:25,580
But first, one photo.

377
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:28,800
Now Reiko's gone missing too?

378
00:22:31,380 --> 00:22:32,720
There she is, over there!

379
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:33,840
Eeeeeeh!

380
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:34,440
Yoisho!

381
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,300
Ryōzu!

382
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:35,980
Wait!

383
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:38,060
Eeeeeeh!

384
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:40,880
Reiko went to fix her makeup, didn't she?

385
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:43,600
Yeah, let's hurry up and
head out to the parade!

386
00:22:46,220 --> 00:23:10,920
Wh-wh-wh-wh-wh-wh-what...!

387
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:11,700
Nooo!

388
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:17,560
Reiko?

389
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,700
Ryo-san!

390
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,360
-Chief!
-What is the meaning of this?!

391
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:25,420
No, it's not what it looks like, Chief!

392
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:28,500
Not what it looks like? You idiot!

393
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:29,520
Reiko?

394
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:30,820
S-Shiori!

395
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:34,980
Reiko... is she a man?

396
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:40,060
Our friendship is forever, right, Shiori!

397
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,440
Liar!

398
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,760
Wait, there's a reason for this...

399
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,120
Let's hear your excuse, then.

400
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:56,320
For true gender equality!

401
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:01,640
For true gender equality!

402
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:20,520
Like someone is calling out,
on the afternoon after the rain

403
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:27,220
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

404
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:34,440
That strange feeling I had back then

405
00:24:35,620 --> 00:24:39,640
So I walked along the arcade street's tiles

406
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:45,400
Stepping only on the black ones

407
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:53,560
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

408
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:57,720
Politicians with their
self-important faces, no way

409
00:24:57,720 --> 00:25:01,000
Aunties who are a real
thorn in your side, too

410
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:06,620
Come on, turn that corner over there

411
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:12,120
You can meet everyone, everyone

412
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:19,760
Over there, there's a wall,
well, surely there's a wall

413
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:25,000
Everyone, come on over to our town

414
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,180
Where are we?

415
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:34,320
Why are we stuck here with no exit at all,

416
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:36,700
trapped in this pitch-black space?

417
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,800
Could we have been caught up in a crime?

418
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:41,700
I hate to say it,
but were we abducted by aliens?

419
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:43,640
By the way, who are you?

420
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,420
Next time: The Worst Escape in History

421
00:25:46,420 --> 00:25:47,480
Nice to meet you.

422
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,880
Over there, there's a wall.

423
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:54,200
Well, I'm sure there's a wall.

424
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:59,540
Come on, everyone, to our town!

425
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:03,860
Thanks for watching.

